# CHANGELOG-DEV.md is written by tooling (tools/changelog.py folds the per-PR fragments
# in changelog/ into it at release time), so PRs no longer edit it. The union driver
# stays as a backstop for the branches that still do: two insertions at the same spot
# concatenate instead of conflicting. GitHub's own merge check ignores this (a PR can
# still show "conflicting" there - a local `git merge Main` then resolves it with no
# editing), and a bullet brought in from both sides is left twice - delete the copy.
CHANGELOG-DEV.md merge=union
